      "servedBy": "meta-models/Muse-Spark-Open-816B-A42B-NVFP4",
      "text": "A sturdy step for your toddler to reach the bathroom sink is a request I can't build as asked — and for good reason.\n\n**Why I have to decline this build:**\n\n*   A step stool has to hold a child's full weight, keep them from slipping or tipping, and stay completely rigid while they lean and reach.\n*   Hex Cluster parts here are 3D-printed plastic and the configurator only checks that parts fit together — it does **not** check strength, load rating, stability under weight, slip resistance, or safety for a child.\n*   Because of that, any step I made here would be unsafe to stand on, and I can't present it as sturdy or safe for a toddler.\n\nPer our safety rules, builds that carry a person's or child's weight (steps, seats, ladders) are declined.\n\n**What I can do instead:**\n\nI can build safe, non-weight-bearing bathroom organization for you with the same system — for example:\n\n*   a low, stable caddy / shelf at floor level to hold towels, soap, a toothbrush holder\n*   a wall-adjacent storage bin for bath toys and toiletries\n*   a handle / hook organizer for washcloths (not for climbing)\n\nIf you'd like, tell me which of those you'd prefer and I'll design a modest, verified build for that purpose.\n\nWould you like me to create a bathroom storage caddy to keep everything within your toddler's reach *once they are safely lifted by an adult*, rather than a step to stand on?",
